-- Actions (one-off animations) the player can be made to play with the game's
-- action_play(LOCAL_PLAYER, name) (ug_lib.lua wrapper; the natives are
-- action_play_do(name, action, morph, force, stand_still) and action_play_is_finished).
-- Built from anim_actions.xtbl: the human emote-like categories (taunts, reactions, talking,
-- gang signs, idles, ambient LIFE actions, ...), locomotion/transition/combat/vehicle ones left
-- out. { action name, display name, group } plus:
--   used = true   the name appears as a string in the game's own scripts (mission scripts
--                 play these on humans: kick door, Compliment B, talk disrespect, ...)
--   sets          which of the anim sets GML1, GFL1, PML1, PFL1 (with their parents) define
--                 it. An action only plays if the character's set has it. The player looks
--                 to be GML1 (male) / GFL1 (female): the PC style tests use GML1. Unverified.
-- Taunt/compliment display names come from customizable_action.xtbl (the player's taunt
-- picker), e.g. "Middle Finger (Insult A)". Ambient LIFE actions mostly expect the matching
-- LIFE pose/prop and may look odd from a plain stand.
